            "title": "Exception handling",
            "text": "Exception handling manages errors that happen while a program runs, letting the program continue or stop gracefully instead of crashing."
          },
          {
            "type": "checkpoint",
            "mode": "self_check",
            "prompt": "Why handle exceptions instead of letting the program crash?",
            "explanation": "So the program can show a helpful message, recover or stop cleanly, making it more robust for users."
          },
